		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Auto off function]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4599&amp;p=37526#p37526"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Is there a way to implement APO if the battery level gets below a set value? <br>It would be nice to use the radio for automatic transmissions without user input, and make sure the battery doesn't fully die.<br><br>Example usecase:<br>Hiking in a remote area, radio is used for APRS TX with an APRS mode, that transmits location automatically. When the battery gets to 50%, the radio turns off, so it will be available for communcation later. It would be even better if the radio could do a series of actions once a battery has drained to a level: turn of GPS, select a different channel (without APRS or any auto transmission).<br><br>Is there anything like this on the roadmap @VK3KYY ?</div></blockquote>These radios are not designed for your use case.<br><br>As I said previously, the firmware can't turn these radios completely off.<br><br>Even if we added a function to put the radio into standby at a specific battery level, the battery would continue to drain. This is especially true of the radios with colour screens. <br><br>If you need APRS and emergency communication, you should use two different radios<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Jun 19, 2025 8:53 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
